  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "d1",
      "phase": 4,
      "subject": "ts-spec-sync",
      "choice": "Accept ts-spec-sync as judged at the outcome gate with no deterministic check serving it on every step; its trust stays uncalibrated until its judge seeds are graded by a signed-in judge (author verify rung 8). A failing grade reaches the step that owns the specs the run edited and never the first step of the run: the engine derives that step from the criteria that serve ts-spec-sync, so only ts-dis-links, ts-plan-spec and ts-code-related serve it.",
      "alternatives": [
        "A person signs off spec agreement on every run",
        "A deterministic check for contradictions between behaviours, which no rule can express",
        "For where a failing grade goes: the criteria of the setup step and of the triage step serve it as well, so the engine sends the run to the earliest of them and one sentence of a spec costs the whole run",
        "For where a failing grade goes: the judge names the place of the defect, which decides nothing at the outcome gate because the engine derives the target from the criteria that serve the final criterion",
        "For where a failing grade goes: a change of the engine's rule so that a named place decides, which the package cannot make"
      ],
      "consequence": "Until rung 8 has run and the outcome judge is accepted, a contradiction between specs can pass the outcome gate on the judge's word alone; ts-dis-links (one definition per id), ts-plan-spec (judged at the plan gate) and ts-code-related (judged at the code gate) are the earlier lines of defence. A failing grade costs the step that owns the specs and what follows it, not the whole run: a run with no full discovery goes to the plan step, and the quick lane, which plans and edits no spec, goes to the code step.",
      "decided_by": "agent, on the owner's approval of the blueprint and outcome on 2026-11-21; to be confirmed by the owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "d2",
      "phase": 4,
      "subject": "read_gap and read_component",
      "choice": "Each reading gate (read_gap and read_component) keeps one judge, because the engine asks every model step for one and a gate holds one (spec parallel-reading, PRL-B13 and PRL-B14); the judges of the gates of the seven steps are unchanged.",
      "alternatives": [
        "An engine capability that lets a read-only step go without a judge",
        "A panel of judges for one gate"
      ],
      "consequence": "A visit with N reading sessions holds N more judge sessions, run beside their items; the open question about the judges of one gate stays open in the spec.",
      "decided_by": "agent, on the task's acceptance criterion 3; to be confirmed by the owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "d3",
      "phase": 4,
      "subject": "ts-accepted",
      "choice": "Accept ts-accepted as judged at the outcome gate, with no deterministic check serving it on the two reading units (read_gap and read_component): each has one judge and no check, as the engine asks of a model step and as spec parallel-reading says; their criteria serve it at uncalibrated trust until their judge seeds are graded by a signed-in judge (author verify rung 8).",
      "alternatives": [
        "A check on each reading gate that serves ts-accepted, which could only count the characters of a findings line",
        "No judge on the reading gates, which needs an engine capability the engine does not have"
      ],
      "consequence": "Until rung 8 has run, the findings of a reading session are graded on the judge's word alone; the writing session confirms each finding in the file it names before a document rests on it, and its own check and judge come after.",
      "decided_by": "agent, on the task's acceptance criterion 5; to be confirmed by the owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "d4",
      "phase": 4,
      "subject": "owner_questions, ask_route and ask_owner",
      "choice": "The three units of the owner's pause carry no judge: the unit owner_questions is a script, ask_route a route and ask_owner an ask, and none of them holds a model session (spec owner-questions, OWQ-B1 and OWQ-B2); the triage check verifies the sort and the owner decisions the list is built from, and the answers check of ask_owner refuses a reading called wrong.",
      "alternatives": [
        "A judge on the question list, which could only compare a file a script wrote with the note the script read",
        "A person's sign-off on the list, which the pause itself already is"
      ],
      "consequence": "A list that holds a wrong question is caught by the pause that shows it to the owner and by the deterministic tests of its limits (20 questions, 500 characters), not by a model's reading.",
      "decided_by": "agent, on the task's acceptance criterion 7; to be confirmed by the owner"
    }
  ],
